# Vikunja board reconcile LOG — the `vikunja` skill APPENDS a new dated entry at the END of this file
# after each board reconcile. NEVER rewrite this header, and NEVER edit or reorder an existing entry —
# only add a new one after the last line.
#
# WHY append-only (2026-08-25): every entry used to overwrite one shared header (last_reconciled /
# at_commit / note), so every parallel branch that reconciled the board touched the SAME lines and every
# merge conflicted on this file (see e.g. commits 831a014e9, d4e8f1d71, acb8abe7b, all "# Conflicts:
# docs/.vikunja_sync"). Pure appends at the end let independent branches' reconciles merge cleanly.
#
# What this file is FOR: `tools/gates/vikunja_freshness.py` (CLASS VF) only checks (a) the git-log
# timestamp of the last commit that touched this file at ALL, and (b) whether this file is staged in the
# current commit — it does not parse anything below this header. So any append satisfies the gate; the
# entries below are for humans/Claude (a durable log of what board reconciles happened, when), not the
# gate's logic.
#
# Entry format: `## YYYY-MM-DD  <short label — commit / branch / theme>` then a short note of what was
# reconciled on the board (tasks marked done, labels advanced, duplicates closed). Newest entry LAST.

