## 2026-08-27  one-brain STRICT full-7 batch CLOSED — task #180 marked DONE, description corrected
The strict "all seven merged regions read back at once" check (onebrain_merge_verify --keys all) is now
all_go=true, 7/7 organs GO 6/6 seeds. The prior entry's characterization (a co-residence-dependent nmda_slow
WIRING draw) was itself superseded by direct reproduction: that was the d6_multiref_wm seam, closed separately
by cfg.dedup_synapse_masks (a duplicate-edge per-synapse MASK misalignment, not a receptor-draw issue). The
LAST seam (prospective_memory) was NOT floating-point accumulation as first guessed either -- root cause was
RegionManager.initialize()'s inhibitory-cell selection using one shared RNG stream across regions in list
order (never name-keyed, unlike the wiring/threshold seams), so the SAME firing neuron routed to g_e in one
arm and g_i in the other purely from co-residence. Fixed via cfg.per_region_inhibitory_seed (additive,
default-off, byte-identical-when-off). #180 updated + marked DONE. #171 (4-organ pool#1+pool#2 byte-identity)
and #177 (cross-region integration) untouched, remain their own rungs. Branch research/pmem-fp-accumulation-
full7 (not yet merged to main). Findings: 2026-08-27-dedup-synapse-masks-closes-onebrain-full7-d6-nmda-slow,
2026-08-27-pmem-fp-accumulation-full7-GO.
